"text":"3. Search in google \"cabalex fnf converter\" and convert the chart in there, then put it in a list and follow the code below with your song"},"o_comment":{"blockId":"o","x":12311,"y":6968,"width":200,"height":200,"minimized":false,"text":"play as opponent"},"bFR":{"blockId":null,"x":945,"y":641,"width":370,"height":379,"minimized":false,"text":"Click the block above to delete all of the things prepackaged with the engine\n\nRemember to also delete the costumes and sounds in the \"background\", \"SongPlayer\" and \"Characters\" sprites to save assets and make the project load faster\n\n\n\n\nYou could also delete the \"editors\" sprite to save a lot of assets on the project and increase the load speed\n\n(but remember to re-add it when making changes)"},"bFS":{"blockId":null,"x":1415,"y":640,"width":458,"height":2272,"minimized":false,"text":"---------HOW TO ADD SONGS-----------\n\n1.Add the Inst and Voices (Located in assets/songs) to the \"SongsPlayer\" sprite and name them Inst_*Song* and Voices_*Song*\n\n2.In the editors menu, enter the songs editor and press add song\n\n3.On my engine converter (https://turbowarp.org/1220979078)\nConvert the chart of the song (Located in assets/data/songs)\nand paste all the codes back in the engine\n\n---------HOW TO ADD CHARACTERS------------\n\n1.Add the costumes to the \"Characters\" Sprite (If the names are repeated rename them with a prefix (*Charactername*#) (Example: bf#idle0000)\n\n2.Make sure the costume names of the animations end with 0000, 0001, 0002, etc\n\n3.In the editors menu, enter the characters editor, click \"file\" and \"new character\" (You could also convert the character json located in assets/characters on the converter and click import)\n\n4.Click \"anim\" and start adding animations \n(Main ones are idle,singleft,singright,singdown,singup,danceleft,danceright,singleftmiss,singdownmiss,singupmiss and singrightmiss)\n\n5.Make sure to check when putting the costume name when adding an animation \n(Example, bf's idle costume is named \"BF idle dance0000\" , so you put \"BF idle dance\"\n\n6.Change the healthbar color, size and offsets of each animation in the editor\n\n7.Add the icons in the \"healthbar/icons\" sprite named as:\n*Character*_1  (Neutral)\n*Character*_0  (Losing) (Optional)\n*Character*_2  (Winning) (Optional)\n\n--------HOW TO ADD STAGES-----------\n\n1.In the editors menu, enter the stage editor and click \"file\" and then \"new stage\"\n\n2.Add the stage elements as costumes to the \"Background\" sprite\n\n3.For each element, click \"sprite\" and then \"add new\" and enter the name of the costume (make sure there are no repeated ones or ones that are the name of the stage)\n\n4.To edit a sprite, click on the sprite, then in the editor click \"sprite\" and you can drag it to move it, change the size, layer, etc\n\n5.You can also change the size of the characters in the stage and drag them to move them\n\n\n--------HOW TO ADD CUSTOM NOTES-------\n\n!!You can view the custom notes on the chart editor, clicking \"file\" then \"view n type\"!!\n\n1.Add the custom note costumes to the \"ChartNotes\" sprite and name them accordingly (Example for left note, which is \"1\"):\n1_\"CustomNote\"                      (Normal)\n1_hold_\"CustomNote\"             (Hold)\n1_holdend_\"CustomNote\"       (Hold end)\n\n2.In the editors menu, enter the notes editor and click \"file\" and \"add custom note\"\n\n3.Open the custom note and change the metadata of said custom note\n\n4.Trick!!!! if your character contains especial animations (lets say \"singleft-beatbox\" or \"singdown-beatbox\") you can change the animation of said custom note to be \"sing\" followed by the special thing (Example: singbeatbox)\n\n----------HOW TO ADD NOTESKINS-------\n\n1.Change the noteskin in the metadata of the song in the chart editor\n\n2.Add the notes to the sprites \"StrumNotes\" and \"ChartNotes\" And name them accordingly (Examples for left note):\n\n(Left being 1, down 2, up 3 and right 4)\n\n-In strumnotes- \n1_0_\"Noteskin\"        (Grey Note)\n1_3_\"Noteskin\"        (Glow animation 1)\n1_2_\"Noteskin\"        (Glow animation 2)\n1_1_\"Noteskin\"        (Glow animation 3)\n1_4_\"Noteskin\"        (Press animation 1)\n1_5_\"Noteskin\"        (Press animation 2)\n\n-In Chartnotes-\n1_\"Noteskin\"                   (Normal)\n1_hold_\"Noteskin\"          (Hold)\n1_holdend_\"Noteskin\"    (Holdend)\n\n3.You can also add custom particles for each noteskin, just follow the same names as the costumes but with the sufix \"_*Noteskin*\"\n\nsplash1_pixel\nhold1_pixel\nholdend1_pixel\n\n4.Same thing with the judgments\n"}},"currentCostume":0,"costumes":[{"name":"costume1","bitmapResolution":1,"dataFormat":"svg","assetId":"91223aa32e565265e90daf5e427a5795","md5ext":"91223aa32e565265e90daf5e427a5795.svg","rotationCenterX":0,"rotationCenterY":0}],"sounds":[],"volume":100,"layerOrder":6,"visible":true,"x":0,"y":0,"size":100,"direction":90,"draggable":false,"rotationStyle":"all around"},{"isStage":false,"name":"Notes//StrumNotes","variables":{"Arlxrq+!AVVaT(eCln(E":["⭕Note ID",5],"*$f=.sPh?GFp!18|WSf3":["⭕Note Side","1"],"JmS~Jmvgu0Or/:8Groa}":["⬆️Notes sides","1"],";}0Bsbhld^jPx]g4SgD:":["#Yoffset","0"],"Gkd~8/1rP=lZB2UH=nS+":["⭕Note Side",0],"WrfT6CVXiRoX7gAljrAn":["#COSTUME","c"],"07nJxGU*I;)Fkh!,/!Q8":["⭕Note ID",0],"v@xtnge4F``JN:N|){4p":["#COSTUME",0]},"lists":{},"broadcasts":{},"blocks":{"v,":{"opcode":"operator_and","next":null,"parent":"v-","inputs":{"OPERAND1":[2,"e?"],"OPERAND2":[2,"a*["]},"fields":{},"shadow":false,"topLevel":false},"e?":{"opcode":"operator_gt","next":null,"parent":"v,","inputs":{"OPERAND1":[3,[12,"⭕Note Ms2","+W4x(#qm3Ylew?R4_f}~"],[10,""]],"OPERAND2":[3,"a*]",[10,"-300"]]},"fields":{},"shadow":false,"topLevel":false},"a*]":{"opcode":"operator_multiply","next":null,"parent":"e?","inputs":{"NUM1":[3,[12,"⭕Milliseconds gap2","!F*1{OaLt3P2H?/ncS,2"],[4,""]],"NUM2":[1,[4,"-1"]]},"fields":{},"shadow":false,"topLevel":fal